lled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api and paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the failure (about 18% error rate across all regions), the rollback to v2.3.0, and the next steps.\n\nI haven't checked whether the error rate has recovered since the rollback. The next step is to confirm that and investigate v2.3.1 before it is released again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01F96Kbg3nWH2euC3cGFiDAJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012PGuTa2fXffCSffMzCe3tS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging only. I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CX1Fwrbjc6Db64Kit7SpwB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01A4e37rv7Hpo5jqpxFwMxnE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 release", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate ~18%, all regions: us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release healthy in production, in all production regions. Rollback status: rolled_out, verified, all three regions now on v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production; v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Next steps: confirm error rate recovery, investigate v2.3.1 failure before any re-release.", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api and paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the failure (about 18% error rate across all regions), the rollback to v2.3.0, and the next steps.\n\nI haven't checked whether the error rate has recovered since the rollback. The next step is to confirm that and investigate v2.3.1 before it is released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}